##### 🧑‍🚀 4.14 Owner Intelligence Module (Personal & Exclusive Feature)
**Access:** Single sign-in only for the product owner (Shubham). No other users can access this module.

**Purpose:** Your personal “intelligence system” – a live rocket telemetry-like experience during active launches, similar to a “live launch slider” but focused on rocket parts and movement.

**Key Features:**
- **Real Rocket Telemetry Slider / Live Launch View**  
  - When a launch is active (detected via Launch Library 2 or SpaceX API), display a **horizontal or vertical progress slider** representing mission timeline (T-0, Max-Q, MECO, Stage Separation, Fairing Separation, SECO, etc.).
  - **Dynamic part highlighting:** As the launch progresses (based on available time/phase data), automatically highlight or animate moving rocket parts (e.g., booster engines firing, stage separation, payload deployment).
  - Show real-time or near-real-time parameters where available: altitude, velocity, downrange distance, acceleration, stage status, etc.
  - Visuals: Annotated 3D/2D rocket model (from Rocket Systems Explorer) with parts lighting up or moving in sync with telemetry phases.

- **Data Sources & Limitations (Realistic):**
  - Use public APIs: Launch Library 2 for launch status/events, SpaceX public API (`/launches/latest`, `/launches/upcoming`) for basic timeline and vehicle data.
  - For telemetry-like data: Pull from public SpaceX webcast-derived sources or historical patterns when live data is limited. Full raw telemetry (altitude/speed streams) is rarely public in real-time due to regulations, so combine:
    - Official webcast timeline events.
    - Simulated/estimated telemetry using known rocket profiles (Falcon 9, GSLV, etc.) from Rocket Systems Explorer.
    - Any open telemetry endpoints (e.g., historical SpaceX telemetry repos if still active).
  - Fallback: Manual or AI-assisted phase progression if exact live data is unavailable.

- **Self-Updating Mechanism:**
  - Backend cron jobs or WebSocket/polling that automatically refreshes launch status every 10–30 seconds during active launches.
  - The slider and part highlights **self-update** in real-time (or near real-time) without manual refresh.
  - Auto-detect when a launch goes live and push notification/alert to the owner dashboard.

- **Additional Owner Tools:**
  - Private dashboard showing only your personal notes, saved analyses, and custom rocket configurations.
  - One-click “Simulate My Rocket” that feeds into the Virtual Rocket Builder (Phase 4).

**Technical Notes:**
- Protected via simple, secure single-user authentication (e.g., password + email, or JWT-based with hardcoded owner credentials). No public registration for this module.
- Frontend: Real-time updates using WebSockets (FastAPI + React/Streamlit) or Server-Sent Events.
- Disclaimer to owner: “Telemetry is approximated from public sources where full real-time data is restricted.”

##### 📝 4.15 Notes & Ideas Session
**Purpose:** A collaborative space for discussing platform improvements, new features, and space-related ideas.

**Features:**
- **Private Owner Notes:** Your personal section for saving ideas, feature requests, bug notes, and analysis (tied to Owner Intelligence Module).
- **Public Ideas Board (Anonymous Contribution):** 
  - Any visitor can submit ideas anonymously (no login required for submission).
  - Ideas appear as cards with title, description, category (e.g., Visualization, Failure Analysis, New Rocket, UI), and vote count.
  - Moderation: Only the owner can approve, hide, or comment on public ideas.
- **Discussion Threading:** Simple comments on ideas (anonymous or logged-in for owner).
